{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Is YHWH among us, or not (אם אין).</b> The verse ought to have said 'if not' (אם לא), as in (Exodus 16:4) 'הילך בתורתי אם לא.' But it alludes to the attribute called אין ('nothing'), which is called יראה (awe), and second to it is that which is called יש ('being'), which is called חכמה (wisdom) — and this is what is said (Job 28:12): 'והחכמה מאין תמצא.' Therefore Scripture joined YHWH to it and said, 'היש YHWH' — this is the matter that Jacob said (Genesis 28): 'אכן יש YHWH,' and it is the saying of Solomon, of blessed memory (Proverbs 8:21): 'להנחיל אוהבי יש.' And you already know that one cannot separate wisdom from awe, and to this the masters of truth alluded in saying: if there is no awe there is no wisdom; if there is no wisdom there is no awe — for all is bound and unified, this in that. Now Israel separated them here, and cut and planted, and therefore they were punished immediately: 'ויבא עמלק.' And understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:25.211293356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}